From: VelaSights BK7258 port
Subject: [PATCH] nsh: allow dispatching the first builtin command

builtin_isavail() returns a zero-based builtin index.  Treating index zero as
unavailable prevents the first builtin command from running directly from
NSH, for example `renew wlan0` when renew is the first generated builtin.

diff --git a/apps/nshlib/nsh_command.c b/apps/nshlib/nsh_command.c
--- a/apps/nshlib/nsh_command.c
+++ b/apps/nshlib/nsh_command.c
@@ -1272,2 +1272,2 @@
-  if (index > 0)
+  if (index >= 0)
     {
--
2.43.0
